window.TIMELINE_TOUR = [{"t":"Start with the key","go":"Timeline Key (how to read the chart)","x":"Green boxes are anchors of history that tie the seven timelines together. Arrows link one verse to another. A zig-zag means time has been compressed so the lines stay in step. Words in parentheses marked ref explain a verse; they are not the verse itself."},{"t":"Israel in exile, 605 B.C.","go":"Israel in Exile, 605 B.C.","x":"The chart opens where Daniel’s visions open. Nebuchadnezzar takes Jerusalem, and what Jesus later called “the times of the Gentiles” begins (Lk 21:24). Babylon, Medo-Persia, Greece, and Rome follow in the order Daniel was given (Dan 2; Dan 7)."},{"t":"The seventy weeks of Daniel","go":"70 weeks of Daniel","x":"Gabriel gave Daniel a count of seventy weeks of years for his people and his city (Dan 9:24). Sixty-nine run from the command to rebuild Jerusalem to Messiah the Prince (Dan 9:25). After them Messiah is cut off (Dan 9:26). One week, seven years, remains."},{"t":"The cross","go":"The cross","x":"Every line on the chart passes through this point. “For Christ also hath once suffered for sins, the just for the unjust, that he might bring us to God…” (1 Pet 3:18). Here Satan was defeated (Col 2:15), and from here the gospel goes out to every nation (Matt 28:19–20)."},{"t":"The last days in the church","go":"Last Days in the church","x":"Paul described the close of the church age: men lovers of their own selves, “Having a form of godliness, but denying the power thereof…” (2 Tim 3:5). The letter to Laodicea is the picture of it (Rev 3:14–17)."},{"t":"Israel reborn","go":"Israel reborn, 1948","x":"Isaiah asked, “…shall a nation be born at once?…” (Isa 66:8). On May 14, 1948, after nineteen centuries, Israel was a nation again, and in 1967 Jerusalem returned to Jewish hands. God is not done with Israel (Rom 11:1, 29)."},{"t":"The rapture of the church","go":"Rapture of the Church","x":"This is the next event for the believer, and no sign must come before it. “…the dead in Christ shall rise first: Then we which are alive and remain shall be caught up together with them in the clouds, to meet the Lord in the air…” (1 Thess 4:16–17). In heaven the judgment seat of Christ follows (2 Cor 5:10)."},{"t":"The seven-year covenant","go":"Seven-year covenant","x":"A ruler confirms a covenant with many for one week, seven years (Dan 9:27). Daniel’s seventieth week begins with it, and the Day of the Lord with it. The first four seals follow: false peace, war, famine, and death (Rev 6:1–8)."},{"t":"The middle of the week","go":"Mid-Covenant","x":"He breaks the covenant, stops the sacrifice, and sits in the temple claiming to be God (Dan 9:27; 2 Thess 2:4). Jesus called it the abomination of desolation and told those in Judaea to flee (Matt 24:15–16). Satan is cast down to the earth (Rev 12:9), and the mark is enforced (Rev 13:16–17)."},{"t":"The great tribulation","go":"Great Tribulation","x":"“For then shall be great tribulation, such as was not since the beginning of the world to this time, no, nor ever shall be” (Matt 24:21). The seventh seal opens into the seven trumpets and the seventh trumpet into the seven bowls, so all three finish together (Rev 8:5; 11:19; 16:18)."},{"t":"The King returns","go":"Jesus returns","x":"“Behold, he cometh with clouds; and every eye shall see him…” (Rev 1:7). He comes with the armies of heaven (Rev 19:11–16), and His feet stand on the mount of Olives (Zech 14:4). Armageddon ends by the word of His mouth, and the beast and the false prophet are cast alive into the lake of fire (Rev 19:20)."},{"t":"The thousand years","go":"Millennium","x":"Satan is bound (Rev 20:1–3) and Christ reigns from Jerusalem, and believers reign with Him (Rev 20:6). The wolf dwells with the lamb (Isa 11:6), and the earth is full of the knowledge of the LORD (Isa 11:9). From here Israel’s line and the believer’s run woven together."},{"t":"The great white throne","go":"Great White Throne judgement","x":"When the thousand years end, Satan is loosed, the last rebellion is put down by fire from heaven, and the devil is cast into the lake of fire (Rev 20:7–10). Then the unsaved dead stand before God. “And whosoever was not found written in the book of life was cast into the lake of fire” (Rev 20:15). Fallen man’s line and Satan’s end here."},{"t":"All things made new","go":"All things made new","x":"“And I saw a new heaven and a new earth…” (Rev 21:1). The New Jerusalem comes down, God dwells with men, “…and there shall be no more death…” (Rev 21:4). Heaven’s line and the earth’s meet here."},{"t":"The gospel","go":"The Gospel: ABC's of Salvation","x":"The chart ends where the book ends. There are two endings, and the way to the right one is a Person. “For whosoever shall call upon the name of the Lord shall be saved” (Rom 10:13)."}];
